FORMAT: 1A
HOST: https://shelter.example.com

# Shelter API

An animal shelter: pets and their adoption (MFI-16.4 fixture).

# Group Pets

## Pets Collection [/pets{?status}]

+ Parameters
    + status (enum[string], optional) - Filter by adoption status.
        + Members
            + available
            + adopted

### List pets [GET]

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Headers

            X-Total-Count: 2

    + Attributes (array[Pet])

### Add a pet [POST]

+ Request Minimal (application/json)
    + Attributes (Pet)

+ Response 201 (application/json)
    + Attributes (Pet)

+ Response 422 (application/json)
    + Attributes (Error)

# Group Adoptions

## Adoption [/pets/{id}/adoption]

+ Parameters
    + id (number, required) - The pet's id.

### Adopt a pet [POST]

+ Response 204

# Data Structures

## Pet (object)
+ id: 1 (number, required) - Unique pet id.
+ name: Rex (string, required) - The pet's name.
+ status (enum[string]) - Where the pet is.
    + Members
        + available
        + adopted

## Cat (Pet)
+ indoor: true (boolean) - Whether the cat stays inside.

## Problem (object)
+ message: Invalid pet (string, required) - What went wrong.

## Error (object)
+ Include Problem
+ code: 422 (number) - The status code.
